# Send these from Visual Studio: click "Send request" above each one, top to bottom.
# Replace YOUR_PASSWORD before sending, and put it back before committing.

@host = https://localhost:7269

### Is the server and database OK?
GET {{host}}/health

### Sign in
# @name login
POST {{host}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "userName": "snj",
  "password": "snj1",
  "deviceId": "my-laptop",
  "deviceName": "My laptop"
}

### Who am I, and what may I do?
GET {{host}}/api/v1/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### All permissions
GET {{host}}/api/v1/permissions
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### All roles
GET {{host}}/api/v1/roles
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### Create a role
POST {{host}}/api/v1/roles
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Viewer",
  "description": "Can see users and roles",
  "permissions": ["users.view", "roles.view"]
}

### All users
GET {{host}}/api/v1/users
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.accessToken}}
